---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Doc from '../components/legal/Doc.astro';
const updated = '30 October 2026';
// Shows a draft note and keeps the page out of search until the placeholders are filled (design/legal/README.md).
const draft = true;
---

<Base title="Data processing addendum · Comarket" description="How Comarket handles a brand's Stripe customer data as its service provider." stage="none" noindex={draft}>
  <Doc
    title="Data processing addendum"
    lede="To decide whether a sale counts, we check buyers against your Stripe customers. We do that only for you, under these rules."
    updated={updated}
    draft={draft}
    current="/dpa"
    toc={false}
  >
    <h2>1. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.1</span>This addendum is part of the <a href="/brand-terms">Brand Agreement</a> between [[LEGAL ENTITY NAME]]
      ("Comarket") and the brand. It covers the personal information Comarket receives from the brand's connected Stripe
      account ("Customer Data"). If it conflicts with the Brand Agreement, this addendum applies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="n">1.2</span>For Customer Data, the brand is the business (controller) and Comarket is its service provider
      (processor), as the California Consumer Privacy Act and similar state laws use those terms.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What we process, and why</h2>
    <div class="tbl">
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Whose</th><td>The brand's Stripe customers, and buyers who start a checkout from a Storefront</td></tr>
          <tr><th>What</th><td>Email, phone number, card fingerprint (a code Stripe derives from a card, never the card number), Stripe customer and subscription IDs, and payment, refund and dispute records for Storefront checkouts</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Why</th><td>Only to decide whether a buyer is new, credit the sale to a creator, and calculate fees and reversals under the Brand Agreement</td></tr>
          <tr><th>How long</th><td>Email, phone and card fingerprint: until the check for that checkout is done. Customer and subscription IDs: until the Commission Period and Refund Window end. Then deleted</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>3. Our commitments</h2>
    <p><span class="n">3.1</span>Comarket will:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>process Customer Data only for the purposes above and on the brand's instructions in the Brand Agreement and its settings;</li>
      <li>not sell or share it, or use it for advertising, for any other customer, or outside our relationship with the brand;</li>
      <li>not combine it with data from other sources, except as the law allows a service provider to;</li>
      <li>not keep a copy of the brand's customer list, and never give Customer Data to creators;</li>
      <li>bind everyone who handles it to confidentiality;</li>
      <li>protect it with reasonable security: encryption in transit and at rest, access limited to people who need it, multi-factor sign-in, and the narrowest Stripe permissions that do the job;</li>
      <li>use only service providers bound by similar terms (today Cloudflare for hosting and Neon for the database), tell the brand 30 days before adding one, and stay responsible for them;</li>
      <li>help the brand answer consumer privacy requests about Customer Data, and pass on any we receive;</li>
      <li>tell the brand within 72 hours of confirming a security breach affecting Customer Data, and help it respond;</li>
      <li>tell the brand if we can no longer meet these commitments, and let it take reasonable steps to stop any unauthorized use; and</li>
      <li>delete Customer Data within 30 days after the Brand Agreement and the last Commission Period end, unless the law requires us to keep it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <span class="n">3.2</span>We certify that we understand and will comply with these restrictions. On reasonable request, once a
      year, we'll answer the brand's written questions about how we meet them.
    </p>

    <h2>4. The brand's commitments</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">4.1</span>The brand confirms it may share Customer Data with us for these purposes, and that its privacy policy
      tells buyers it uses service providers to check new customers and credit referrals.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Customers outside the US</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">5.1</span>If the GDPR or UK GDPR applies to Customer Data, this addendum is intended to meet Article 28, and the
      European Commission's standard contractual clauses (Module 2, with the UK addendum where needed) apply to the transfer to
      Comarket in the United States.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      <span class="n">6.1</span>The limits of liability in the Brand Agreement apply to this addendum. Questions go to
      <a href="mailto:[[CONTACT EMAIL]]">[[CONTACT EMAIL]]</a>.
    </p>
  </Doc>
  <Footer />
</Base>
